it caused heavy damage to several properties, primarily metal barns, right along State Highway 78. As it continued east-northeast, it crossed FM 981 where a single family home was damaged, including broken windows and loss of roof shingles and decking, along with a windshield shattered on a vehicle. It continued northeast from there, causing sporadic tree damage as it headed towards a business located on CR 4965. At this business, a triple wide manufactured building was shifted off of its cement block base, and the metal siding and roof was pulled off of a building located next to it. The tornado continued northeast, damaging trees, and is believed to have lifted before crossing US 69. The maximum wind rating for this tornado was 95 mph.","source":"NWS Storm Survey","state":"TX","torLengthMi":3.28,"torScale":"EF1","torWidthYd":150.0,"type":"Tornado","wfo":"FWD"},{"begin":"2022-03-14T23:15Z","county":"Anderson","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-03-14T23:15Z","endLat":31.75,"endLon":-95.62,"episode":167240,"id":1012292,"injuries":0,"lat":31.75,"location":"0.59 E Palestine","lon":-95.62,"magnitude":1.5,"narrative":"A CoCoRahs observer reported quarter to ping pong ball sized hail in Palestine, TX.","source":"CoCoRaHS","state":"TX","type":"Hail","wfo":"FWD"},{"begin":"2022-03-14T23:15Z","county":"Ellis","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-03-14T23:15Z","endLat":32.3,"endLon":-96.58,"episode":167240,"id":1012293,"injuries":0,"lat":32.3,"location":"2.23 NW Alma","lon":-96.58,"magnitude":1.25,"narrative":"A trained spotter reported half dollar sized hail along Interstate 45 near the Buc-ees in Ennis, TX.","source":"Trained Spotter","state":"TX","type":"Hail","wfo":"FWD"},{"begin":"2022-03-14T23:17Z","county":"Fannin","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"50.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-03-14T23:17Z","endLat":33.3901,"endLon":-96.2436,"episode":167240,"id":1013682,"injuries":0,"lat":33.395,"location":"1.